          {
            "operation": "replace",
            "base_lines": [
              10,
              10
            ],
            "target_zero_based_slice": [
              9,
              10
            ],
            "before": "Code baseline: `e11c07ce90318309f058c8097ffd1c440a8ffb84`.\r\n",
            "after": "Code baseline: `c819bec432446dd3c9b1edf1583384cfe76c6c71`.\r\n"
          },
          {
            "operation": "replace",
            "base_lines": [
              149,
              151
            ],
            "target_zero_based_slice": [
              148,
              150
            ],
            "before": "is entrywise nonnegative. In a submultiplicative matrix norm, the series is\r\nbounded by \\(\\sum_k(\\beta\\|B\\|)^k/k!=e^{\\beta\\|B\\|}\\), so it converges.\r\nEach summand has nonnegative entries. This establishes a positivity statement for\r\n",
            "after": "is entrywise nonnegative. Finite dimensionality ensures convergence under declared assumptions, and\r\neach summand has nonnegative entries. This establishes a positivity statement for\r\n"
          },
          {
            "operation": "delete",
            "base_lines": [
              271,
              278
            ],
            "target_zero_based_slice": [
              269,
              269
            ],
            "before": "The integrated expansion is nevertheless absolutely convergent. A spin\r\nspecies occupying \\(k\\) of the three sites has \\(k(3-k)\\leq2\\) allowed\r\nhops, so each occupation state has at most four outgoing hops across both\r\nspins. There are at most \\(64\\cdot4^n\\) rooted closed \\(n\\)-hop sequences,\r\nand each has magnitude at most \\(\\beta^n/n!\\) because \\(E\\geq0\\).\r\nThus the absolute sum is bounded by \\(64e^{4\\beta}\\). This is a\r\nconvergence bound, not an equal-weight pairing or a sampling-cost result.\r\n\r\n",
            "after": ""
          },
          {
            "operation": "replace",
            "base_lines": [
              346,
              349
            ],
            "target_zero_based_slice": [
              336,
              338
            ],
            "before": "baseline named above identifies the repository snapshot inspected for this\r\nreview. The package manifests and\r\n[current review receipt](docs/preprint_review_validation_2026_10_02.json)\r\nbind the revised package bytes; historical source hashes retain their dates.\r\n",
            "after": "baseline named above supplies the exact repository revision for the sources\r\ndiscussed here.\r\n"
          },
          {
            "operation": "replace",
